# Resume Tool implementation

When the user asks to implement, continue, or work on the **Resume Tool / Resume Tailoring / Resume Editor** feature:

1. This is **not** ordinary feature work. Follow [`docs/RESUME_TOOL_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](docs/RESUME_TOOL_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md) only.
2. **One Cursor chat = exactly one implementation phase.** After that phase, update [`docs/RESUME_TOOL_PROGRESS.md`](docs/RESUME_TOOL_PROGRESS.md) and **stop**. Do not start the next phase in the same chat, even if the plan says a later phase is “eligible.”
3. At session start, read (in addition to other project rules):
   - `docs/RESUME_TOOL_ARCHITECTURE.md`
   - `docs/RESUME_TOOL_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`
   - `docs/RESUME_TOOL_PROGRESS.md`
4. Use those files plus the actual repository to choose the earliest incomplete phase. If progress and the repo disagree, ask Edwin. Do not skip gates.
5. If progress says implementation is **not** approved, or status is `AWAITING MANUAL VERIFICATION` / `BLOCKED`, do not begin a new phase unless Edwin is only reporting verification results for the parked phase.
6. Never mark a phase `COMPLETE` in the progress file until Edwin has reported required manual verification (Word, production HTTPS, UI walkthroughs, human checkpoints) as passed.
7. Do not implement Resume application code while the planning docs still say planning-only **and** progress says not approved.

Do not apply this one-phase rule to unrelated domains (cooking, career applications, school, fitness, etc.).
